    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Solve \\( x^2 = -16 \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>Since \\( i^2 = -1 \\),<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}x^2 &= -16 = 16 i^2\\\\x &= \\pm 4i.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(x=\\pm 4i\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Evaluate \\( i^{33} + i^{34} \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>The powers of \\( i \\) repeat every four: \\( i^1=i,\\; i^2=-1,\\; i^3=-i,\\; i^4=1 \\).<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}i^{33}&=(i^4)^8\\cdot i=i,\\\\i^{34}&=(i^4)^8\\cdot i^2=-1.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\(i^{33}+i^{34}=i-1=-1+i.\\)</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(-1+i\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Compute \\( (4,\\,-2)+(1,\\,5)-(2,\\,-1) \\) in the form \\( (x,\\, y) \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>Addition and subtraction of ordered pairs are componentwise:<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}(4,-2)+(1,5)-(2,-1)&=(4+1-2,\\; -2+5-(-1))\\\\&=(3,\\,4).\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\((3,\\,4)\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find the product \\( (3,\\,-1)(2,\\,4) \\) in the form \\( (x,\\, y) \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>The product of ordered pairs is \\( (x_1,y_1)(x_2,y_2)=(x_1x_2-y_1y_2,\\; x_1y_2+y_1x_2) \\).<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}(3,-1)(2,4)&=(3\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 4,\\; 3\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 2)\\\\&=(6+4,\\; 12-2)=(10,\\,10).\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\((10,\\,10)\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Using ordered pairs, show that \\( i^2 = -1 \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>By definition \\( i=(0,1) \\) and \\( -1=(-1,0) \\).<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}i^2=(0,1)(0,1)&=(0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 1,\\; 0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0)\\\\&=(-1,\\,0)=-1.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(i^2=-1\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Express \\( (2-i)-(3+4i)+i \\) in the form \\( a+bi \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>Collect real and imaginary parts:<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}(2-i)-(3+4i)+i&=2-3+(-1-4+1)i\\\\&=-1-4i.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(-1-4i\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find the multiplicative inverse of \\( z=1-2i \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>Multiply numerator and denominator by the conjugate \\( 1+2i \\):<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}z^{-1}&=\\frac{1}{1-2i}=\\frac{1+2i}{(1-2i)(1+2i)}\\\\&=\\frac{1+2i}{1+4}=\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{2}{5}i.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(\\dfrac{1}{5}+\\dfrac{2}{5}i\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Express \\( \\dfrac{3+i}{1+i} \\) in the form \\( a+bi \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>Multiply numerator and denominator by \\( 1-i \\):<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3+i}{1+i}&=\\frac{(3+i)(1-i)}{(1+i)(1-i)}\\\\&=\\frac{3-3i+i-i^2}{2}=\\frac{3-2i+1}{2}\\\\&=\\frac{4-2i}{2}=2-i.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(2-i\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find \\( |z| \\) if \\( z=(1+2i)(2-i) \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>Use \\( |z_1 z_2|=|z_1|\\,|z_2| \\).<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}|1+2i|&=\\sqrt{1+4}=\\sqrt{5},\\\\|2-i|&=\\sqrt{4+1}=\\sqrt{5},\\\\|z|&=\\sqrt{5}\\cdot\\sqrt{5}=5.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(5\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find the conjugate of \\( z=(2+i)(1-3i) \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>First expand \\( z \\):<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}z&=(2+i)(1-3i)=2-6i+i-3i^2\\\\&=2-5i+3=5-5i.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br>Hence \\( \\bar{z}=5+5i \\).<br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(5+5i\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "If \\( z=1+i \\), find \\( |z| \\) and the principal argument \\( \\theta \\) (\\( -\\pi<\\theta\\le\\pi \\)).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}|z|&=\\sqrt{1^2+1^2}=\\sqrt{2},\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\quad\\sin\\theta=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\implies\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\( |z|=\\sqrt{2} \\), \\( \\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4} \\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Express \\( z=\\sqrt{3}-i \\) in trigonometric form with \\( -\\pi<\\theta\\le\\pi \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}r&=\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3})^2+(-1)^2}=\\sqrt{3+1}=2,\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\quad\\sin\\theta=-\\frac12\\implies\\theta=-\\frac{\\pi}{6}.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\(z=2\\Bigl(\\cos\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\Bigr)+i\\sin\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\Bigr)\\Bigr).\\)</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(2\\bigl(\\cos(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6})+i\\sin(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6})\\bigr)\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Express \\( z=-1+i \\) in trigonometric form with \\( -\\pi<\\theta\\le\\pi \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}r&=\\sqrt{(-1)^2+1^2}=\\sqrt{2},\\\\\\cos\\theta&=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\quad\\sin\\theta=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\implies\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\(z=\\sqrt{2}\\Bigl(\\cos\\frac{3\\pi}{4}+i\\sin\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\Bigr).\\)</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(\\sqrt{2}\\bigl(\\cos\\dfrac{3\\pi}{4}+i\\sin\\dfrac{3\\pi}{4}\\bigr)\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find the product of \\( z_1=3\\bigl(\\cos\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}+i\\sin\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\bigr) \\) and \\( z_2=2\\bigl(\\cos\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}+i\\sin\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\bigr) \\) in trigonometric form.",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>Use \\( z_1 z_2=r_1 r_2\\bigl(\\cos(\\theta_1+\\theta_2)+i\\sin(\\theta_1+\\theta_2)\\bigr) \\).<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}z_1 z_2&=6\\Bigl(\\cos\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\Bigr)+i\\sin\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\Bigr)\\Bigr)\\\\&=6\\Bigl(\\cos\\frac{5\\pi}{12}+i\\sin\\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\Bigr).\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(6\\bigl(\\cos\\dfrac{5\\pi}{12}+i\\sin\\dfrac{5\\pi}{12}\\bigr)\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find \\( \\dfrac{z_1}{z_2} \\) where \\( z_1=6\\bigl(\\cos\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}+i\\sin\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}\\bigr) \\) and \\( z_2=3\\bigl(\\cos\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}+i\\sin\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\bigr) \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>Use \\( \\dfrac{z_1}{z_2}=\\dfrac{r_1}{r_2}\\bigl(\\cos(\\theta_1-\\theta_2)+i\\sin(\\theta_1-\\theta_2)\\bigr) \\).<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{z_1}{z_2}&=2\\Bigl(\\cos\\Bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{6}-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\Bigr)+i\\sin\\Bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{6}-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\Bigr)\\Bigr)\\\\&=2\\Bigl(\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{3}+i\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\Bigr).\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(2\\bigl(\\cos\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}+i\\sin\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\bigr)\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "If \\( z=2\\bigl(\\cos\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}+i\\sin\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\bigr) \\), find \\( z^2 \\) in trigonometric form.",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>By De Moivre's theorem, \\( \\bigl[r(\\cos\\theta+i\\sin\\theta)\\bigr]^n=r^n(\\cos n\\theta+i\\sin n\\theta) \\).<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\(z^2=4\\Bigl(\\cos\\frac{2\\pi}{3}+i\\sin\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\Bigr).\\)</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(4\\bigl(\\cos\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}+i\\sin\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}\\bigr)\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "If \\( z=2\\bigl(\\cos\\bigl(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\bigr)+i\\sin\\bigl(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\bigr)\\bigr) \\), find \\( z^{-1} \\) in trigonometric form.",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>The inverse is \\( z^{-1}=\\dfrac{1}{r}\\bigl(\\cos(-\\theta)+i\\sin(-\\theta)\\bigr) \\).<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\(z^{-1}=\\frac12\\Bigl(\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{6}+i\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\Bigr).\\)</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(\\dfrac12\\bigl(\\cos\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}+i\\sin\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\bigr)\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find the distance between the points representing \\( z_1=3+i \\) and \\( z_2=-1+4i \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>The distance is \\( |z_1-z_2| \\).<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}z_1-z_2&=(3+i)-(-1+4i)=4-3i,\\\\|4-3i|&=\\sqrt{16+9}=5.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(5\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Solve \\( x^2-2x+2=0 \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>Complete the square:<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}x^2-2x+2&=0\\\\x^2-2x+1&=-1\\\\(x-1)^2&=-1=i^2\\\\x-1&=\\pm i\\\\x&=1\\pm i.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(x=1\\pm i\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find the real and imaginary parts of \\( \\dfrac{1}{2-i} \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2-i}&=\\frac{2+i}{(2-i)(2+i)}=\\frac{2+i}{5}\\\\&=\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{1}{5}i.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br>Real part \\( \\dfrac{2}{5} \\), imaginary part \\( \\dfrac{1}{5} \\).<br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; real \\( \\dfrac{2}{5} \\), imaginary \\( \\dfrac{1}{5} \\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "If \\( (2x+1,\\, y-3)=(5,\\, 1) \\), find \\( x \\) and \\( y \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>Two ordered pairs are equal if and only if corresponding components are equal.<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}2x+1&=5\\implies x=2,\\\\y-3&=1\\implies y=4.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(x=2,\\; y=4\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find \\( z^{-1} \\) if \\( z=3+4i \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}z^{-1}&=\\frac{3-4i}{(3+4i)(3-4i)}=\\frac{3-4i}{9+16}\\\\&=\\frac{3}{25}-\\frac{4}{25}i.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(\\dfrac{3}{25}-\\dfrac{4}{25}i\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Express \\( z=-\\sqrt{3}+i \\) in trigonometric form with \\( -\\pi<\\theta\\le\\pi \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}r&=\\sqrt{3+1}=2,\\\\\\cos\\theta&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\quad\\sin\\theta=\\frac12\\implies\\theta=\\frac{5\\pi}{6}.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\(z=2\\Bigl(\\cos\\frac{5\\pi}{6}+i\\sin\\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\Bigr).\\)</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(2\\bigl(\\cos\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}+i\\sin\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}\\bigr)\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Evaluate \\( i^{100}+i^{101}+i^{102}+i^{103} \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}i^{100}&=(i^4)^{25}=1,\\\\i^{101}&=i,\\\\i^{102}&=-1,\\\\i^{103}&=-i.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\(1+i-1-i=0.\\)</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(0\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find the square roots of \\( z=9(\\cos\\pi+i\\sin\\pi) \\) in trigonometric form.",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>The square roots are \\( w_k=\\sqrt{9}\\bigl(\\cos\\dfrac{\\pi+2k\\pi}{2}+i\\sin\\dfrac{\\pi+2k\\pi}{2}\\bigr) \\) for \\( k=0,1 \\).<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}k=0:\\quad &3\\Bigl(\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{2}+i\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\Bigr),\\\\k=1:\\quad &3\\Bigl(\\cos\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\Bigr)+i\\sin\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\Bigr)\\Bigr).\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\( 3\\bigl(\\cos\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}+i\\sin\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\bigr) \\) and \\( 3\\bigl(\\cos(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2})+i\\sin(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{2})\\bigr) \\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "If \\( z=\\cos\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}+i\\sin\\dfrac{\\pi}{4} \\), find \\( z^8 \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>By De Moivre's theorem,<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\(z^8=\\cos 2\\pi+i\\sin 2\\pi=1.\\)</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(1\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Convert \\( z=2\\bigl(\\cos\\bigl(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\bigr)+i\\sin\\bigl(-\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\bigr)\\bigr) \\) to the form \\( a+bi \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}z&=2\\Bigl(\\frac12-i\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\Bigr)\\\\&=1-\\sqrt{3}\\, i.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(1-\\sqrt{3}\\, i\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "If \\( z=-5+12i \\), find \\( \\bar{z} \\) and \\( |z| \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\\bar{z}&=-5-12i,\\\\|z|&=\\sqrt{(-5)^2+12^2}=\\sqrt{25+144}=13.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\( \\bar{z}=-5-12i \\), \\( |z|=13 \\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Given \\( z_1=-1+2i \\), compute \\( z_1^2-2z_1+1 \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br>Note that \\( z_1^2-2z_1+1=(z_1-1)^2 \\).<br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}z_1-1&=-2+2i,\\\\(z_1-1)^2&=(-2+2i)^2=4-8i+4i^2\\\\&=4-8i-4=-8i.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\(-8i\\)</div>"
  },
  {
    "type": "math_show",
    "q": "Find \\( z\\bar{z} \\) if \\( z=6-8i \\), and hence write \\( |z| \\).",
    "c": "<strong>Solution</strong><br><br><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\\[\\begin{aligned}z\\bar{z}&=(6-8i)(6+8i)=36+64=100,\\\\|z|&=\\sqrt{z\\bar{z}}=10.\\end{aligned}\\]</div><br><br><div style=\"display:inline-block;border:2px solid #00D5FF;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin-top:6px;\"><strong>Answer</strong> &nbsp; \\( z\\bar{z}=100 \\), \\( |z|=10 \\)</div>"
  }
]
